      "text": "The \"best\" CRM for a small agency depends heavily on your business model: are you delivering marketing campaigns and funnels for clients, selling high-ticket consulting retainers, or bridging the gap between closing deals and project delivery?\n\n---\n\n### 1. Best for Digital Marketing & Lead-Gen Agencies: **GoHighLevel (HighLevel)**\nIf you build funnels, run ads, set up lead automations, or want to give clients their own portals, GoHighLevel is virtually the industry standard for agencies. It is designed specifically for agencies rather than single businesses.\n\n* **Why it fits agencies:** You can spin up separate sub-accounts for every client under a single subscription. It replaces Calendly, ClickFunnels, Mailchimp, and Zapier in one stack.\n* **Pricing:**\n  * **Starter:** $97/month (~$81/month billed annually) \u2014 up to 3 sub-accounts.\n  * **Agency Unlimited:** $297/month (~$248/month billed annually) \u2014 unlimited sub-accounts and client portals.\n  * **Agency Pro (SaaS Mode):** $497/month (~$414/month billed annually) \u2014 allows you to fully white-label and resell the CRM as software to your clients.\n* **Watch out for:** The user interface can feel clunky, and there are additional pay-as-you-go costs for SMS, phone numbers, and AI credits.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Best for Smooth Project Delivery & Retainers: **monday Sales CRM**\nAgencies rarely stop at \"Deal Won\" \u2014 you immediately have to onboard the client and execute deliverables. monday Sales CRM seamlessly connects pipeline management directly to project management.\n\n* **Why it fits agencies:** When a deal closes, it can automatically trigger client onboarding boards, task templates, and creative production timelines in the same workspace.\n* **Pricing (billed annually, 3-seat minimum):**\n  * **Basic:** ~$12 per user/month (lead/deal management).\n  * **Standard:** ~$17 per user/month (two-way email sync, custom templates, automations).\n  * **Pro:** ~$28 per user/month (sales forecasting, email tracking, mass emails).\n* **Watch out for:** Has a strict 3-user minimum, so solopreneur agencies still pay for three seats.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Best for Pure Inbound Marketing & Brand Authority: **HubSpot**\nHubSpot offers an intuitive interface, deep integrations, and top-tier contact tracking. If your agency runs on content marketing, SEO, and thought leadership, HubSpot is a classic choice.\n\n* **Why it fits agencies:** Its free tier is one of the most generous on the market for pure contact and pipeline tracking.\n* **Pricing:**\n  * **Free Tools:** $0 (contact records, deal pipelines, form capture, basic email marketing).\n  * **Starter Customer Platform:** Starts at ~$15\u2013$20/seat/month (removes HubSpot branding, adds simple email automation and lead routing).\n  * **Professional Tiers:** Jumps to ~$800\u2013$890/month base (plus mandatory ~$3,000 onboarding fees).\n* **Watch out for:** The infamous \"pricing cliff\". It is very affordable at the Free/Starter level, but scaling into HubSpot Pro can be cost-prohibitive for a small boutique agency.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Best for Simple, High-Ticket Sales Pipelines: **Pipedrive**\nIf your agency sells custom, high-ticket retainer contracts and you just need reps (or the founder) to stay on top of follow-ups, Pipedrive is simple and clutter-free.\n\n* **Why it fits agencies:** It is strictly an activity-based pipeline CRM. No confusing menus; it keeps your active proposals and contract negotiations moving forward.\n* **Pricing (billed annually):**\n  * **Lite:** ~$14 per user/month (lead, calendar, and pipeline management).\n  * **Growth:** ~$39 per user/month (full email sync, automated follow-ups, scheduler).\n  * **Premium:** ~$59 per user/month (custom reporting, revenue forecasting, contract e-signatures).\n* **Watch out for:** It does not handle client project delivery or advanced email newsletters; you will need separate tools (like Asana, ClickUp, or Mailchimp) connected via Zapier.\n\n---\n\n### Decision Matrix: Which one should you pick?\n\n| If your agency priority is... | Choose... | Realistic monthly cost |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Managing/reselling tech stacks & funnels for clients** | **GoHighLevel** | $97 \u2013 $297/mo flat |\n| **Connecting closed deals directly into project workflows** | **monday Sales CRM** | $51 \u2013 $84/mo (for 3 seats) |\n| **Simple, reliable sales deal tracking & follow-ups** | **Pipedrive** | $28 \u2013 $78/mo (for 2 seats) |\n| **Polished UI, inbound contact capture, clean forms** | **HubSpot (Free/Starter)** | $0 \u2013 $40/mo (for 1\u20132 seats) |",
